0..56 Comment "//! What is open crosses back from a migration as bytes."
57..60 Comment "//!"
61..137 Comment "//! A crossing asks two judgements. Mobility is authority: nothing the value"
138..213 Comment "//! holds is meaningful only where it was made. Openness is representation:"
214..289 Comment "//! the value names no location, so its bytes read the same at every world."
290..366 Comment "//! They agree on data and part at a handle, which is mobile always and open"
367..393 Comment "//! when what it holds is."
394..397 Comment "//!"
398..475 Comment "//! Each declaration below migrates to the seat and returns its result to the"
476..550 Comment "//! operator. Data of integers is open, and so is a handle to it. A closed"
551..627 Comment "//! thunk is open too, since it captures nothing. A field the operator reads"
628..679 Comment "//! from what comes back reads as it does in place."
680..683 Comment "//!"
684..696 Comment "//! - cites:"
697..797 Comment "//!   [Rainey-2026-localmem_typedirected_adaptive_serialization_location_contentaddressable_memory],"
798..820 Comment "//!   § 5.1, openness"
821..887 Comment "//! - cites: [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5], § 3"
888..958 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/worlds/open.gandr` — what is not open stays"
959..1034 Comment "//! - see: #3275 — `projectedDone`, `projectedInner` and `forcedLater`, a"
1035..1085 Comment "//!   field read from a record a migration answers"
1086..1089 Comment "//!"
1090..1329 Comment "//! [Rainey-2026-localmem_typedirected_adaptive_serialization_location_contentaddressable_memory]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3828688 \"Rainey et al., LoCalMem: Type-Directed Adaptive Serialization for Location- and Content-Addressable Memory\""
1330..1497 Comment "//! [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-78663-4_9 \"Murphy, Crary and Harper, Type-Safe Distributed Programming with ML5\""
